0,Walak people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walak_people,"Music uses the goknggaik [id] instrument, and often features the song Wasioayamari (""Let Us Unite""). [6] The dance recounts Papuan ancestors believed to have migrated from Yunnan, via Taiwan, Philippines, Papua New Guinea, and east to Ifala Island, then to Genyem, spreading across Papua.",Walak,Trans-New Guinea
